const p1 = `VERIFY cocond-markov-poincare-ot r0_2 -- check (a) behaviour x geometry fidelity. Read /home/wlia0047/ar57/wenyu/GeneRec/results/research/issue121/trees/round_20261028_221240_652/cocond-markov-poincare-ot/{train_rqvae.py,model/model.py,model/layers.py,model/utils.py,model/__init__.py}. Observed: the active quantization path is model/model.py:26-30 -> model/layers.py:283-289 -> model/layers.py:121 -> model/layers.py:98-104, i.e. pure Euclidean squared-distance argmin (with the original Euclidean Sinkhorn only at the last level, layers.py:106-113). train_rqvae.py:247-248 reads train.parquet only for the 'target' column to select item rows; no session/user sequence, no directed transition matrix, no Markov diffusion, no B_bt/alpha, no Poincare cost, no Klein/Einstein barycenter anywhere (grep for transition|markov|diffus|Einstein|Klein|barycenter|median over the tree returns only an unrelated EMA 'alpha' at layers.py:196-197). model/utils.py:17-59 and 162-329 contain hyperbolic helpers, but grep shows they are referenced only inside utils.py; nothing imports utils into layers/model/__init__, and RQVAE uses model/layers.MLP/RQLayer. So this is an unchanged Euclidean quantizer plus dead hyperbolic code. Verdict: NEEDS_FIX (blocking). Open: check (b) and (c).`;
await tools.progress.append_progress({content:p1});
const p2 = `VERIFY cocond-markov-poincare-ot r0_2 -- check (b) trainability and coupled switch. Static trace of train_rqvae.py:316-330 -> RQVAE.forward -> RQLayer.forward -> VQLayer.forward: the baseline Euclidean path is differentiable (quant_loss at layers.py:132, straight-through at layers.py:133, codebook embed.weight is nn.Embedding parameter at layers.py:62), and loss finiteness is guarded at train_rqvae.py:322-323. But the proposal's coupled pathway does not exist: no three switches (behaviour on/off, curvature on/off) exist in the code, no transition matrix is built or passed, and no Poincare distance/barycenter is applied, so switching behaviour off or replacing curvature with Euclidean is impossible and no SID/gradient change can occur. The only Sinkhorn is the original Euclidean one (layers.py:81-113) gated to self.training and last level only (layers.py:260-261), and export uses infer_use_sk=False (train_rqvae.py:415-417) so exported SIDs are plain argmin. Dead hyperbolic helpers in model/utils.py:162-329 are never in the autograd graph, so no gradient reaches any curved operation. Verdict: NEEDS_FIX (blocking). Open: check (c) integration.`;
await tools.progress.append_progress({content:p2});
return "ok";

